  "content": {
    "id": "p37-q12-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "12",
    "prompt": "A rectangular gallery floor is to be partially carpeted around the edge.\nThe hall is 30 metres wide and 40 metres long.\nThe breadth of the carpeted edge is $x$ metres as shown.\nInside the carpeted area is a rectangular timber floor.\n\nFind an expression in terms of $x$ for the following:",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [
      {
        "id": "p37-q12-diagram",
        "role": "question",
        "format": "tikz",
        "code": "% mathsmap-diagram-colours {\"version\":1,\"kind\":\"geometry\",\"base\":[],\"semantic\":[],\"reference\":\"page 37, p37-q12-diagram\"}\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1cm,y=1cm,every node/.style={font=\\fontsize{10}{12}\\selectfont,text=black}]\n\\special{dvisvgm:raw <metadata data-graph-strokes=\"1\"/>}\n\\draw[black,line width=0.8pt] (0,0) rectangle (4,3);\n\\draw[black,line width=0.8pt] (0.7,0.7) rectangle (3.3,2.3);\n\\draw[black,<->,line width=0.4pt] (2,2.3)--(2,3) node[midway,right] {$x\\,\\mathrm{m}$};\n\\node[align=center] at (2,1.5) {Timber\\\\floor};\n\\node at (2,0.35) {Carpet};\n\\path (0,0)--(4,0) node[midway,below=2mm] {$40\\,\\mathrm{m}$};\n\\path (4,0)--(4,3) node[midway,right=2mm] {$30\\,\\mathrm{m}$};\n\\end{tikzpicture}",
        "src": null,
        "widthMm": 65,
        "alt": "Mathematical diagram",
        "overlayOf": null,
        "transparent": false,
        "axes": null,
        "spec": {
          "sourcePage": 37,
          "sourceRegion": "Upper-right floor diagram",
          "description": "Unshaded, aligned outer and inner rectangles. Outer dimensions are 40 m horizontally and 30 m vertically. A vertical double-headed arrow spans the top carpet border and is labelled x m. Interior labels are Timber floor and Carpet. Source decorative blue outlines are rendered black under the house diagram policy; drawing coordinates are schematic and add no numerical givens.",
          "mathematics": "Uniform border width x on all four sides; timber-floor dimensions are 40−2x and 30−2x.",
          "answerVisibility": "All labels are permanent givens; no answers appear in the question diagram."
        },
        "derived": false,
        "reviewStatus": "needs-review"
      }
    ],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p37-q12-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "The breadth of the timber floor.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(30-2x)\\text{ m}$",
          "worked": "Subtract the carpet breadth from both sides:\n$$\\begin{align*}B&=30-x-x\\\\B&=30-2x\\text{ m}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 12
      },
      {
        "id": "p37-q12-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "The length of the timber floor.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(40-2x)\\text{ m}$",
          "worked": "Subtract the carpet breadth from both ends:\n$$\\begin{align*}L&=40-x-x\\\\L&=40-2x\\text{ m}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 12
      },
      {
        "id": "p37-q12-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "The area of the timber floor.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(4x^2-140x+1200)\\text{ m}^2$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}A&=(30-2x)(40-2x)\\\\A&=1200-60x-80x+4x^2\\\\A&=4x^2-140x+1200\\text{ m}^2\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 20
      },
      {
        "id": "p37-q12-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "Find the value of $x$ if the timber floor area is to be 600 square metres.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=5\\text{ m}$. Reject $x=30$ because the timber-floor dimensions must be positive.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}4x^2-140x+1200&=600\\\\4x^2-140x+600&=0\\\\x^2-35x+150&=0\\end{align*}$$\nHere $a=1$, $b=-35$ and $c=150$.\n$$\\begin{align*}x&=\\frac{-(-35)\\pm\\sqrt{(-35)^2-4(1)(150)}}{2(1)}\\\\x&=\\frac{35\\pm\\sqrt{625}}{2}\\\\x&=\\frac{35\\pm25}{2}\\\\x&=30\\text{ or }5\\end{align*}$$\nThe timber-floor dimensions must be positive, so $0<x<15$. Reject $x=30$; the carpet breadth is $5\\text{ m}$.\nCheck: $(30-2\\times5)(40-2\\times5)=20\\times30=600\\text{ m}^2$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 62
      }
    ],
    "diagramPlacement": "right-of-prompt"
  },
